  "contracts": {
    "original_request": "Original FFX::AllocTex calls FFX::CreateTex for a 1024-square ARGB8888 2D target with flags 0x381. Original OpenGL IDeviceSetRenderTargetFBO interprets bit 8 as implicit GL_DEPTH_COMPONENT24 storage.",
    "native_ownership": "Renderable legacy allocations already retained native depth-24 renderbuffers. Admit bit 8 only on render targets and require retained implicitDepth when sampler flags include it. No allocation backend, signature, feedback, callback or teardown rule was bypassed.",
    "gpu_regression": "Existing three-cycle GPU fixture now uses the original FFX flag combination and independently queries actual depth attachment type, nonzero name, >=24-bit depth and 32x32 extent. It rejects the flag on sampled creation and sampler edits and retains callback/PCT/index/font/shader pixel regressions.",
    "limits": "94 constants and one texture unit remain truthful. Unsupported copy, additional units and model/material contracts remain unavailable."
